(
 ']ListIssues [owner] <project> -html -collapse -verbose -filename= -permanent -assignees='
 ''
 'Alternatively you can specify owner & repo this way: ]GitHub.ListIssues aplteam/TestRepo'
 ''
 'Lists all open issues of the given repo with "issue number" and "title", but check'
 '-verbose and -html.'
 ''
 'You may list all issues of all repos of the given owner with the -allRepos flag.'
 ''
 '-html        Adds date, body & url and creates an HTML page.'
 '             That allows to search all issues in one go.'
 '-filename=   Filename for the HTML created when the -html flag is specified.'
 '             If this is not specified, a temporary filename is used.'
 '-collapse    Makes both the "details" and the "body" of each issue collapsible.'
 '             Is ignored if -html is not specified.'
 '-verbose     Adds more data: labels, creator, create date, assignees and number of comments.'
 '             Is ignored when -html is specified.'
 '-permanent   Saves the given owner in the configuration file. If no owner is specified and'
 '             this flag is specified an error is thrown.'
 '-assignees=  Filters issues accordingly. Requires either -verbose (default) or -html. '
 '             Specify multiple assignees with -assignees=doe,smith or, with the same meaning,'
 '             -assignees=doe∨smith'
)
